                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Loved this game but I can only win if I have a monolopy haha. I played this a bunch in the 90's and loved the realism for essentially owning a Fortune 500 company from the ground up. I believe they even used this in business schools as a learning tool but, its been some time since I remember hearing that. Either way, playing this again was fun and brought me back down memory lane.\n\n\nMY STRATEGY\nStart new game, buy all Timber, internal sale only and make/sell beds. You will only have local competition. Buy all new Timber sources as they appear. One timber source can power the entire map until it is depleted, just put a factory and department store in each city and profit.\n\nThen, research and get VR headsets and buy/own all silica deposits in the game. At that point you can make VR headset factories in each city and utilize your existing department stores you use for selling beds to also sell VR headsets. I was asking $4k each and I still couldn't keep up with demand. Either way, I retired after being the richest man in the world :)",
